    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1: How many times should I brush my teeth with braces? Brush at least three times daily, after meals and before bed. Spend two minutes actively brushing to remove food particles and plaque. 2: Can I use whitening toothpaste while wearing braces? No, avoid whitening toothpaste during treatment. It can cause uneven whitening since toothpaste doesn’t reach areas under the brackets. 3: What kind of toothbrush is best for braces? A soft bristled toothbrush or an electric toothbrush. An electric tooth brush with soft bristles works best. They clean gently around brackets without harming enamel or wires. 4: How can I floss properly with braces? Use a floss threader or water flosser to reach under the wires. It removes food particles without damaging your braces. 5: Why is fluoride toothpaste important? Fluoride toothpaste strengthens enamel, protects against tooth decay, and supports a regular brushing routine during orthodontic treatment. It’s a small step that ensures long-lasting results."
    }
